00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:05.716
An external user need both read and write, but with Guardrails, right.

00:10:05.956 --> 00:10:11.516
The key insight is you need to know
who are using the tool, how they are using it.

00:10:12.636 --> 00:10:14.316
Before you start to build them.

00:10:16.796 --> 00:10:19.436
We've talked about how the agent works.

00:10:20.156 --> 00:10:21.636
Remember the react loop,

00:10:22.596 --> 00:10:25.276
the short term and long term memories, right?

00:10:25.316 --> 00:10:30.236
And also you use the NCP servers to connect to your data store.

00:10:30.716 --> 00:10:37.476
But how do you move from a traditional app
to an Agentic app and evolve your data store?

00:10:38.396 --> 00:10:42.356
Let's come back to the company insurance example, right?

00:10:42.396 --> 00:10:44.876
Who are the users really use this system?

00:10:46.156 --> 00:10:49.756
We have Terry. He's the external user, right.

00:10:49.796 --> 00:10:54.196
He wants to buy car insurance. And then we have NKI.

00:10:54.516 --> 00:10:57.636
She's internal. She's a claim investigator.

00:10:57.836 --> 00:11:01.356
She wants to know and verify the claims accuracy.

00:11:02.596 --> 00:11:05.916
And then we also have Jane. She's a data engineer.

00:11:06.116 --> 00:11:09.276
She builds data products that everyone else use.

00:11:10.276 --> 00:11:18.596
So you think about this. This is one company,
one underlying data, but three very different needs.

00:11:20.316 --> 00:11:26.876
If we want to add Agentic layer into the picture,
every one of them are going to be impacted.

00:11:28.036 --> 00:11:28.836
Let's see how.

00:11:30.636 --> 00:11:34.836
So here you see a very traditional web application, right?

00:11:35.036 --> 00:11:38.716
Terry goes to a web application. Click on something

00:11:39.276 --> 00:11:45.156
and the web application talks to the API's API
connects to the data store.

00:11:46.956 --> 00:11:52.276
It works. It's straightforward.
Now if you add Agentic AI layer into it,

00:11:53.076 --> 00:11:58.436
Terry now is talking to an AI
assistant instead of clicking on the website,

00:11:59.116 --> 00:12:03.116
and that AI assistant connects to NCP servers.

00:12:03.636 --> 00:12:08.396
NCP servers then connect to the same APIs and data store.

00:12:10.116 --> 00:12:12.596
And here's the slide I want you to remember.

00:12:12.636 --> 00:12:15.196
If you take one thing from this talk, let's be.

00:12:15.476 --> 00:12:21.956
This building Agentic AI AI is not
evolutionary. It's not revolutionary.

00:12:22.396 --> 00:12:23.836
It's evolutionary.

00:12:25.196 --> 00:12:29.116
Right? You see, we are using the same APIs.

00:12:29.556 --> 00:12:32.036
You are using the same data stores.

00:12:33.236 --> 00:12:36.756
Basically, you are introducing a new front door.

00:12:37.276 --> 00:12:39.516
Instead of rebuilding the whole house.

00:12:41.636 --> 00:12:48.516
Yeah. So the infrastructure stays.
But there's one thing that becomes even more important

00:12:48.716 --> 00:12:51.916
when the agents are talking to your data.

00:12:52.796 --> 00:12:57.316
If a user clicks a button on your website, you have full control.

00:12:57.796 --> 00:13:05.436
But when the agent picks their own tools in their own order,
governance becomes your safety net.

00:13:07.636 --> 00:13:09.956
Let's see how it works for Jane, for NKI.

00:13:11.076 --> 00:13:14.996
Remember, NKI is the claim investigator, right?

00:13:15.036 --> 00:13:23.716
Her case has three steps. She needs to find the right data
product and retrieve data from the data product she needs,

00:13:24.356 --> 00:13:25.996
and then generate a report.

00:13:27.116 --> 00:13:33.676
So you see on the screen are the tools that can help
Jane NKI complete his her task.

00:13:34.076 --> 00:13:37.636
But That the thing is flow.

00:13:39.036 --> 00:13:44.236
When NKI has to do is discover, access and analyze.

00:13:45.956 --> 00:13:47.556
So what's important to NKI?

00:13:48.956 --> 00:13:52.516
She needs to see the accuracy and quality of data.

00:13:53.556 --> 00:13:56.396
She wants to discover the right data product,

00:13:57.596 --> 00:14:01.076
and she wants to see only the data she's allowed to see.

00:14:01.956 --> 00:14:04.636
Right? And latency is very important.

00:14:04.956 --> 00:14:09.076
She doesn't want to wait
for ten minutes before she can start analyzing.

00:14:10.436 --> 00:14:16.556
Now think about this. If you have an agent
doing those things on behalf of NKI,

00:14:17.716 --> 00:14:26.436
all those things still matters. But maybe even more important,
because the agent is going to move faster than NKI does,

00:14:27.836 --> 00:14:30.076
and your governance has to keep up.

00:14:32.076 --> 00:14:36.956
Now let's flip to Jane. She's the data engineer.

00:14:37.556 --> 00:14:41.596
Her world is different. So data comes from streaming.

00:14:41.596 --> 00:14:48.356
Ingest and Jane are building the pipelines
to transform the data and clean it.

00:14:48.676 --> 00:14:52.796
And then she publishes the data products for everyone else to use.

00:14:54.396 --> 00:14:58.596
She's the one. Make sure the data exists and is trustworthy.

00:14:59.596 --> 00:15:00.000
So what does she care about? Of course,
she cares about the quality, the accuracy of the data as well.

